    "significance": "Intracortical BCIs have achieved remarkable decoding accuracy in the lab, but translating to at-home independent use requires solving stability, drift, self-calibration, and user autonomy. This work shows that a speech and cursor BCI can operate reliably over months in a patient's home without frequent recalibration or constant clinical support, a decisive step toward practical viability. This represents a landmark proof of principle that intracortical BCIs can transition from researcher-managed laboratory experiments to genuine assistive devices, directly addressing the clinical translation barrier that has limited BCI impact.",
